{"schemaVersion":1,"slug":"longest-repeating-character-replacement","title":"Longest Repeating Character Replacement","pattern":"Sliding Window","difficulty":"Medium","leetcode":424,"prompt":"You may change up to k characters in the string to any other letter. Return the length of the longest run of one repeated letter you can produce.","examples":[{"input":"s = \"ABAB\", k = 2","output":"4","why":"Change both A's to B, or both B's to A."},{"input":"s = \"AABABBA\", k = 1","output":"4","why":"Changing one B gives \"AABA\" -> \"AAAA\" as a window of four."}],"constraints":["1 <= len(s) <= 10^5","0 <= k <= len(s)"],"approaches":[{"id":"window","label":"Sliding window","complexity":{"time":"O(n)","space":"O(1)"},"viz":{"s":"array","lo":"pointer:s","hi":"pointer:s","counts":"map"},"layout":{},"source":["def sliding_window(s, k):","    counts = {}","    lo = 0","    most = 0","    best = 0","    for hi in range(len(s)):","        ch = s[hi]","        counts[ch] = counts.get(ch, 0) + 1","        most = max(most, counts[ch])","        while (hi - lo + 1) - most > k:","            counts[s[lo]] -= 1","            lo += 1","        if hi - lo + 1 > best:","            best = hi - lo + 1","    return best"],"variants":[{"id":"typical","label":"Typical","note":null,"result":4,"steps":[{"line":0,"note":null,"ops":[["set",["s"],"AABABBA"],["set",["k"],1]]},{"line":1,"note":null,"ops":[["set",["counts"],{}]]},{"line":2,"note":null,"ops":[["set",["lo"],0]]},{"line":3,"note":null,"ops":[["set",["most"],0]]},{"line":4,"note":null,"ops":[["set",["best"],0]]},{"line":5,"note":null,"ops":[["set",["hi"],0]]},{"line":6,"note":null,"ops":[["set",["ch"],"A"]]},{"line":7,"note":null,"ops":[["set",["counts","A"],1]]},{"line":8,"note":"most is the count of the window's dominant letter.","ops":[["set",["most"],1]]},{"line":9,"note":"costs more than k, the window is illegal and has to give ground.","ops":[]},{"line":12,"note":null,"ops":[]},{"line":13,"note":"A legal window longer than any befo